<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>QUAACK report <%= h run_id %></title>
<style>
  body { font: 16px/1.5 -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color: #1c2430; background: #fff;
         max-width: 62rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; padding-bottom: 0.25rem; border-bottom: 2px solid #d5dbe3; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; }
  p, ul { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  #summary { background: #eef4fb; border-left: 5px solid #2f6fb3; padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; }
  #summary h2 { border: 0; margin-top: 0; }
  #summary p:first-of-type { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  #quaack-bugs { background: #fdecec; border-left: 5px solid #c0392b; padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  #quaack-bugs h2 { border: 0; margin-top: 0; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0.75rem 0; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #d5dbe3; padding: 0.3rem 0.65rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  thead th { background: #f3f5f8; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  td.missing { color: #6d7785; font-style: italic; }
  tr.baseline td { background: #f7f8fa; font-style: italic; }
  table.plan td.step { white-space: nowrap; }
  table.plan .arrow { color: #6d7785; }
  table.plan tr.differs td { background: #fff4d6; }
  table.plan .mark { font-size: 0.8em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #8a5a00; }
  code, pre { font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.9em; }
  code.sql { background: #f3f5f8; border-radius: 3px; padding: 0.05em 0.3em; white-space: pre-wrap;
             overflow-wrap: break-word; -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone; box-decoration-break: clone; }
  pre.sql { background: #f3f5f8; border: 1px solid #d5dbe3; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
            overflow-x: auto; line-height: 1.4; }
  article { margin: 1rem 0 1.75rem; }
  .note { color: #515b69; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  details { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; }
  summary h3 { display: inline; margin: 0; }
  summary .source, summary .fate, summary .warn { display: block; margin-left: 1.1rem; }
  summary .warn { color: #8a5a00; font-weight: 600; }
  /* ::details-content needs Chrome 131+, Safari 18.4+, or Firefox 143+. Older browsers land on the closed section. */
  details.query:target::details-content { content-visibility: visible; }
  details.query:target { outline: 2px solid #2f6fb3; outline-offset: 0.25rem; }
  details.query > pre.sql, details.not-ranked > table { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  svg.funnel { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 0.75rem 0; }
  svg.funnel text { font: 13px -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; fill: #1c2430; }
  svg.funnel text.stage { font-weight: 600; }
  svg.funnel text.counts { font-size: 12px; fill: #515b69; }
  svg.funnel .unknown text.counts { font-style: italic; }
</style>
</head><body>
<h1>QUAACK report <%= h run_id %></h1>
<% unless rule_bugs.empty? %>
<section id="quaack-bugs"><h2>QUAACK bug: a rule made a wrong rewrite</h2>
<p>QUAACK's own rewrite rules are meant to be sound: a rewrite one makes should return the same rows as your query on any data. A test proved each rewrite below wrong, so a rule has a bug. QUAACK dropped these rewrites, and the rest of this report still holds. Please report this, with the names of the rules.</p>
<ul><% rule_bugs.each do |b| %><li><%= h bug(b) %></li><% end %></ul>
</section>
<% end %>
<section id="summary"><h2>The verdict</h2>
<% summary.each do |paragraph| %>
<p><%= h paragraph %></p>
<% end %>
</section>
<section id="queries"><h2>The queries</h2>
<p class="note">Each <code class="sql">$1</code>, <code class="sql">$2</code>, and so on stands for a value from your query. The values themselves never leave your jump server.</p>
<details class="query">
<summary><h3>Your query</h3></summary>
<%= sql(original_sql) %>
</details>
<% rewrites.each do |r| %>
<article class="rewrite"><details class="query" id="<%= h anchor(r["rewrite"]) %>">
<summary><h3><%= h called(r) %></h3> <span class="source">Where it came from: <%= source_html(r) %>.</span> <span class="fate">What became of it: <%= h fate(r) %></span><% if (warn = warning(r)) %> <span class="warn"><%= h warn %></span><% end %></summary>
<% if (assumed = empirical(r)) %>
<p class="empirical"><%= h assumed %></p>
<% end %>
<%= sql(r["sql"]) %>
<% unless atoms(r).empty? %>
<div class="untested"><p><%= h Rewrites::UNTESTED %> <%= h atoms_note(r) %></p>
<% if unchecked_atoms(r).empty? %><details class="untested"><summary><%= h "The #{atoms(r).size} conditions" %></summary><% end %><ul><% atoms(r).each do |a| %><li><%= sql_code(a) %><%= h " (#{Rewrites::CHECKED_LATER})" if checked_later(r).include?(a) %></li><% end %></ul><% if unchecked_atoms(r).empty? %></details><% end %></div>
<% end %>
</details></article>
<% end %>
</section>
<section id="ranking"><h2>Ranking</h2>
<% if winner %>
<p>A candidate is your query, or a rewrite of it, run with a set of new indexes. To be ranked, it must read more than 5% fewer blocks than your query as it is on the slow values (the values from your slow plan), and no more than 5% more on any other set of values. The fewest blocks on the slow values wins.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col" class="num">#</th><th scope="col">Candidate</th><th scope="col" class="num">Blocks read, slow values</th><th scope="col" class="num">Blocks read, all values</th><th scope="col" class="num">Size of its new indexes</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="baseline"><td class="num"></td><td>Your query as it is (the baseline, not ranked)</td><%= baseline.map { num(it) }.join %><%= num("none") %></tr>
<% top.each_with_index do |t, i| %>
<tr class="rank"><td class="num"><%= i + 1 %></td><td><%= h describe(t["label"]) %></td><%= num(t["slow_blocks"]) %><%= num(t["total_blocks_sum"]) %><%= num(Format.size(t["footprint"])) %></tr>
<% end %>
</tbody></table>
<% else %>
<p>Nothing beat your query as it is, so there is no ranking. To be ranked, a candidate must read more than 5% fewer blocks than your query as it is on the slow values (the values from your slow plan), and no more than 5% more on any other set of values.</p>
<% end %>
<% unless unranked.empty? %>
<h3>Measured, and not ranked</h3>
<details class="not-ranked">
<summary>Show the <%= h Words.count(unranked.size, "thing") %> QUAACK tried that didn't pan out</summary>
<table id="not-ranked"><thead><tr><th scope="col">What it was</th><th scope="col">Who proposed it</th><th scope="col">Why it didn't make the cut</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<% unranked.each do |what, who, why| %>
<tr><td><%= h what %></td><%= who ? "<td>#{h who}</td>" : MISSING %><td><%= h why %></td></tr>
<% end %>
</tbody></table>
<p class="note">Who proposed it is who proposed the rewrite. QUAACK doesn't record who thought of each index, so for your query with new indexes it says <%= h Words::MISSING %>. It also says that for a rewrite whose source this run didn't record, or that's missing from what QUAACK's jump server sent.</p>
</details>
<% end %>
<% top.each_with_index do |t, i| %>
<article class="candidate"><h3><%= i + 1 %>. <%= h describe(t["label"]) %></h3>
<% if (r = rewrite_of(t["label"])) %>
<p>Its SQL is under <a href="#<%= h anchor(r["rewrite"]) %>"><%= h Words.lower(called(r)) %></a>, above.</p>
<% end %>
<% unless (measured(t["label"]) || {}).fetch("indexes", []).empty? %>
<p>Its new indexes:</p>
<ul><% measured(t["label"])["indexes"].each do |name| %><li><%= sql_code(indexes.dig(name, "ddl") || name) %></li><% end %></ul>
<% end %>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Values</th><th scope="col" class="num">Blocks read</th><th scope="col" class="num">Your query as it is</th><th scope="col" class="num">Already in memory</th><th scope="col" class="num">Read from disk</th><th scope="col">Against your query</th><th scope="col">Note</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<% measurement_rows(t["label"]).each do |set, *counts, verdict, note| %>
<tr><td><%= h set %></td><%= counts.map { num(it) }.join %><td><%= h verdict %></td><td><%= h note %></td></tr>
<% end %>
</tbody></table>
</article>
<% end %>
</section>
<% if winner %>
<section id="explanation"><h2>Why the winner reads fewer blocks</h2>
<p><%= h describe(winner["label"]) %> <%= h compared %> <%= h CACHE %></p>
<% measured_plan = (measured(winner["label"]) || {})["plan"] %>
<% winner_plan = measured_plan || ((r = rewrite_of(winner["label"])) && r["plan"]) %>
<% if winner_plan && plans_differ?(original_plan, winner_plan) %>
<p class="note"><%= h Plans::MARKED %></p>
<% end %>
<p>How Postgres runs your query now:</p>
<%= plan_table(original_plan, winner_plan) %>
<p class="note"><%= h Plans::BLOCKS_NOTE %></p>
<% if measured_plan %>
<p>How it runs <%= h Words.lower(describe(winner["label"])) %>, as QUAACK measured it on the slow values:</p>
<%= plan_table(measured_plan, original_plan) %>
<% else %>
<p><%= h NO_MEASURED_PLAN %><%= " #{h ESTIMATED_PLAN}" if winner_plan %></p>
<% if winner_plan %>
<p>How it runs <%= h Words.lower(called(r)) %> with no new indexes:</p>
<%= plan_table(winner_plan, original_plan) %>
<% end %>
<% unless (measured(winner["label"]) || {}).fetch("indexes", []).empty? %>
<p>The plan with the new indexes: <%= h Words::MISSING %>.</p>
<% end %>
<% end %>
</section>
<% end %>
<% if negative %>
<section id="negative-result"><h2>Why nothing beat your query</h2>
<h3>The rewrites</h3>
<% if rewrites.empty? %>
<p>QUAACK kept no rewrite to test.</p>
<% else %>
<ul id="negative-rewrites"><% rewrites.each do |r| %><li><%= h fate_line(r) %></li><% end %></ul>
<% end %>
<h3>Indexes the planner wouldn't use</h3>
<% if negative["declined"].empty? %>
<p>The planner would have used every index QUAACK thought of.</p>
<% else %>
<p>QUAACK asked the planner about each of these before building anything. An index is listed once, with every query it was tried for.</p>
<table id="declined-indexes"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Index</th><th scope="col">Tried for</th><th scope="col">Why not</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<% negative["declined"].each do |d| %>
<tr><td><%= d["ddl"] ? sql_code(d["ddl"]) : h("an index QUAACK couldn't write out") %></td><td><%= h searches(d) %></td><td><%= h declined(d) %></td></tr>
<% end %>
</tbody></table>
<% end %>
<h3>Indexes QUAACK thought of that you already have</h3>
<% if negative["existing"].empty? %>
<p>None of the indexes QUAACK thought of already existed.</p>
<% else %>
<p>If QUAACK's best idea is an index you already have, the query isn't slow for lack of an index.</p>
<table id="existing-indexes"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Index</th><th scope="col">Tried for</th><th scope="col">Your index that covers it</th><th scope="col" class="num">Its size</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<% negative["existing"].each do |e| %>
<tr><td><%= e["ddl"] ? sql_code(e["ddl"]) : h("an index QUAACK couldn't write out") %></td><td><%= h searches(e) %></td><td><%= (by = e.dig("covered_by", "name")) ? sql_code(by) : "" %></td><%= num(Format.size(e.dig("covered_by", "size_bytes"))) %></tr>
<% end %>
</tbody></table>
<% end %>
</section>
<% end %>
<section id="indexes"><h2><%= winner ? "Proposed indexes" : "Indexes QUAACK built and measured" %></h2>
<% [[proposed, winner ? "None of the ranked candidates needs a new index." : nil], [unproposed, nil]].each_with_index do |(names, none), i| %>
<% if i == 1 && winner && !names.empty? %>
<h3>Other indexes QUAACK built and measured</h3>
<p>QUAACK built these too, and no ranked candidate uses them.</p>
<% end %>
<% if names.empty? %>
<% if none %><p><%= h none %></p><% end %>
<% if i == 1 && indexes.empty? %><p>QUAACK built no indexes.</p><% end %>
<% else %>
<table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Index</th><th scope="col" class="num">Built size</th><th scope="col">Your index that already covers it</th><th scope="col">Your indexes it would make redundant</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<% names.each do |name| %>
<%= built_row(name) %>
<% end %>
</tbody></table>
<% end %>
<% end %>
<p class="note">Each size is real: QUAACK built the index on a copy of your data. Sizes of your own indexes come from Postgres's statistics.</p>
</section>
<section id="accountability"><h2>Who proposed what</h2>
<h3>Rewrites</h3>
<table id="accountability-rewrites"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><% Accountability::REWRITE_COLUMNS.each do |c| %><th scope="col" class="num"><%= h c %></th><% end %></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<% rewrite_account.each do |name, *counts| %>
<tr><th scope="row"><%= h name %></th><%= counts.map { count_cell(it) }.join %></tr>
<% end %>
</tbody></table>
<p class="note">A rewrite not kept is one QUAACK dropped before it was stored: it was over the limit (five from the LLM, ten from QUAACK's rules), assumed something QUAACK can't check or your data doesn't hold, failed the checks on what goes in, didn't plan, returned different columns, or couldn't have its clock pinned, or, for one of QUAACK's own, repeated another. What became of each rewrite it kept is under the queries, above.</p>
<h3>Indexes</h3>
<table id="accountability-indexes"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Source</th><% Accountability::INDEX_COLUMNS.each do |c| %><th scope="col" class="num"><%= h c %></th><% end %></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<% index_account.each do |name, *counts| %>
<tr><th scope="row"><%= h name %></th><%= counts.map { count_cell(it) }.join %></tr>
<% end %>
</tbody></table>
<p class="note">Proposed, already existed, and planner ignored or couldn't try count the ideas of each search, for your query and for each rewrite, so an idea that came up in two searches counts twice. Built and measured, not better, and ranked count each index QUAACK built once.</p>
<p class="note">Planner ignored or couldn't try also counts the ideas QUAACK couldn't try, because HypoPG, which it uses to try an index without building it, couldn't create them. The planner was never asked about those.</p>
<% if overlap? %>
<p class="note">An index more than one source proposed counts in each of their rows, so the rows by source can add up to more than all sources together.</p>
<% end %>
<p class="note">An index counts as not better only if no candidate that ran with it beat your query. A built index whose candidate beat your query and still wasn't ranked (it tied with a smaller one, or three others did better), or whose candidate timed out, is counted only under built and measured. So the last two columns needn't add up to it.</p>
<% if unrecorded? %>
<p class="note">&ldquo;Not recorded&rdquo; means this run didn't count it. It doesn't mean none.</p>
<% end %>
</section>
<section id="burndown"><h2>Burndown: how much QUAACK did, and where ideas dropped out</h2>
<% [["index", "Index ideas for your query", index_rows], ["rewrite", "Rewrites", rewrite_rows]].each do |id, title, rows| %>
<h3><%= h title %></h3>
<%= funnel(id, title, rows) %>
<table id="burndown-<%= id %>"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col" class="num">Came in</th><th scope="col">Added</th><th scope="col">Dropped</th><th scope="col" class="num">Set aside</th><th scope="col" class="num">Went on</th><th scope="col">Also counted</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<% rows.each do |name, record, stage| %>
<tr><th scope="row"><%= h name %></th><%= stage_cells(record, stage) %></tr>
<% end %>
</tbody></table>
<% end %>
<h3>LLM calls</h3>
<ul id="llm-calls"><% llm_lines.each do |line| %><li><%= h line %></li><% end %></ul>
<p class="note">These are the calls this run of quaack made. If you resumed the run, they leave out the calls made before it stopped.</p>
<h3>Other work</h3>
<ul id="burndown-totals"><% total_lines.each do |line| %><li><%= h line %></li><% end %></ul>
</section>
</body></html>
